{
 "model": "claude-opus-5-5, 2026-10-31 (Claude Code subagent by hand, prompt table-schema/3; trial builds run locally)",
 "notes": [
  "Input: 02-rekordok/output.json (1083 records), apply.py, paths.py, build.py, 0003-target-record-format.md.",
  "Numbered in document order: the printed tables (Industries and applications, two parts lists, two dimension tables, Standards of compliance, Flow coefficients, Torque values, Product code) and also the text sections whose records state valve properties (page-2 design/safety sections, Features and benefits, Pressure/temperature ratings notes, Seat materials, page-12 digital section), so that their facts get the valve as subject instead of 'document'. Only the title block (document type, document code) stays a document statement.",
  "Subject is the valve everywhere except the parts lists (tables 5, 6), where the part name is the subject (default_role subject, kind 'part') with properties Item and Material.",
  "Valve size 'DN 15 (NPS 1/2)' is one condition (valve size) in the dimension, flow and torque tables; valve series F51/F52 is a condition. The size-range subheading ('Sizes DN15 to DN50 ...') is a condition only for the parts lists; in the dimension tables it is ignored because every row carries its own DN size.",
  "Dimension letters are kept as printed ('Dimension A' ...); what a letter measures is only in the drawing (03-abrak). Two-value cells (footnote 1: tolerance limits) are separate maximum/minimum properties; the column groups 'Stem' and 'L/R Thread and Depth' are property suffixes, normalised by property_keys.",
  "Product code (table 14): 'Code X' is a property_with_condition (property 'Code', condition product code option = X) and the position heading ('2. Variant') a suffix, so each option becomes 'Product code position N (...)' with the option letter as condition and its meaning as value.",
  "Seat materials (table 8): the seat heading ('Delrin (D)') is a condition seat material; maximum temperature rating is then a valve property under that condition. Pressure/temperature ratings (table 7): 'Group 1.2/2.2' is a condition material group; the chart curve-list and axis records are skipped (covered by the chart record from 04).",
  "Torque values in Nm and lbf·in are not merged by the program (torque is not a merge family), so each torque fact appears once per unit."
 ],
